// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | CURRENT_DECISIONS
// task: Webhook Trigger Configuration UI | date: 2026-03-04

#what_changed
=routes/webhook.routes.ts: NEW public unauthenticated route POST /webhooks/:workflowId
~Loads workflow, validates trigger:webhook node exists
~Optional HMAC-SHA256 signature validation via X-Hub-Signature-256 header
~Executes workflow with {type: 'webhook', source: IP, data: requestBody}
~Returns 202 Accepted with executionId
=server.ts: IMPORT webhookRoutes; REGISTER after notificationRoutes
=NodeConfigPanel.tsx: 'webhook-url' added to FieldConfig.type union
=NODE_CONFIG_SCHEMAS: trigger:webhook schema with _webhookUrl + webhookSecret fields
=webhook-url renderer: Read-only input + copy-to-clipboard button (checks workflowId exists)

#tech_implications
~Public endpoint — NO requireAuth preHandler — external callers can trigger workflows
~HMAC validation optional: only enforced if webhookSecret configured on trigger node
~Timing-safe comparison prevents signature timing attacks
~JSON.stringify(request.body) used as signed payload (standard for JSON callers)
~workflowId display requires Redux workflow.workflowId selector (muted message if null)
~apiConfig.baseUrl sourced from NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL env var

#constraints
~Workflow must be isEnabled=true; returns 404 otherwise
~Trigger node type must be trigger:webhook; returns 422 if missing
~Secret validation case-sensitive; timing-safe comparison used
~URL display only shows after workflow saved (workflowId must exist in Redux state)
~Copy button uses navigator.clipboard.writeText() (requires HTTPS in production)
